    "Signals in online evaluations are categorized into computed signals and captured signals.",
    "Computed signals require calculation or analysis to derive their value.",
    "Examples of computed signals include faithfulness scores, answer relevance, correctness, hallucination, toxicity, bias, and fairness.",
    "Computed signals are not directly observable and need to be computed based on collected data.",
    "Raw data from conversations is used to generate computed metrics through algorithms or formulas.",
    "Captured signals are directly observed and stored without the need for calculation.",
    "Examples of captured signals include user feedback like thumbs up or thumbs down, latency, and cost per conversation.",
    "Captured signals are recorded as they occur, allowing for easy tracking of chatbot performance.",
    "Understanding the distinction between computed and captured signals is crucial for evaluating chatbot performance."
] 

